module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.CoordinateBlowupSmooth
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.QuasiFinite.ResidueField
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalDoublePoints.BlowUpResidueField
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalDoublePoints.ExceptionalFromChart
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The centre of the next blowup, produced inside a standard affine chart

A rule for choosing the centres of a sequence of blowups at closed points,
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep`, has to produce at every stage a closed point of the blowup
lying over the centre, with unchanged residue field, at which the extension of the maximal ideal
of the centre is generated by the image of the chosen element. The conditions on the local rings
are available once the point is known to lie in the standard affine chart of the blowup attached
to a section `a` of the blown-up ideal: that is [Stacks, Tag 0BFL], registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_affineBlowupStandardOpen_iff_exceptionalIdeal_stalk_eq_span`, together
with `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.map_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_blowupChart` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_germ_residue`.

This file produces such a point, from a prime of the coordinate ring of the chart, and transports
the chart ring to the point. The chart `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι` is an open immersion, so
the stalk of the blowup at a point of it is the local ring of the affine blowup algebra
`Γ(X, U)[I(U)/a]` there, and the map induced on stalks by the blowup morphism is the structure
map of that algebra followed by its localization. All four of the conditions on the point which
do not mention the property carried along the sequence then become statements about the chart
ring:

* lying over the centre is a statement about the prime the chosen prime contracts to;
* the residue field is unchanged exactly when the sections over `U` generate the residue field of
  the chart ring at the chosen prime, which for a maximal prime is its quotient there;
* closedness follows from the previous condition, by [Stacks, Tag 01TE];
* the exceptional condition is [Stacks, Tag 0BFL], whose chart-membership hypothesis is automatic
  for a point of the chart.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.germ_comp_stalkMap_blowupChartι`: **the stalk of the blowup at a point of
  the chart is the local ring of the chart ring there**, compatibly with the structure map from
  the base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι_mem_range_relativeProjChart` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase_blowupChartι`: a point of the chart satisfies the membership
  hypothesis of Tag 0BFL, and its image in the base is the prime it contracts to.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_blowupChartι`: **the residue field at a point of the
  chart is the residue field of its image in the base**, from surjectivity onto the quotient of
  the chart ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isClosed_singleton_of_isIso_residueFieldMap`: a point with unchanged residue
  field over a closed point is closed.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.exists_next_of_chart`: **the four conditions of a rule for
  choosing the next centre which do not mention the carried property, at once**, for a stage of a
  sequence of blowups at closed points.

## Implementation notes

The chart morphism is `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/MoreMorphisms/CoordinateBlowupSmooth.lean`, together with its
structure morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι_comp_blowUpToBase`; nothing about the chart
itself is redefined here.

`AlgebraicGeometry.germ_comp_stalkMap_blowupChartι` proves the factorization of the germ map
through the chart ring for an *abstract* chart inside its own proof, and then applies that to the
chart of the blowup. Two reasons: the concrete instance of the argument does not fit one
heartbeat budget, exhausting it at `whnf`; and the general statement would duplicate the
`private` helper `germ_stalkMap_of_affine_factorization` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ReesAlgebra/ChartMembership.lean`, which is not reachable
by name from another module and which this file may not change. De-privatising it there is the
proper fix, and would let the `have` be deleted.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Tag 0BFL is registered on the equivalence in
`Blowup/ReesAlgebra/ChartMembership.lean`, Tag 0804 on the chart identification in
`Blowup/ReesAlgebra/AffineCharts.lean`, and Tag 01TE on the closedness criterion in
`Morphisms/QuasiFinite/ResidueField.lean`; what is here is their composition with the choice of
a point, which formalizes no tag of its own. Nothing in this file mentions the dimension formula
`dim_κ(𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹) = 2n + 1` of Section 54.12, so no hypothesis of that kind is carried.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BFL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BFL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01TE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01TE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGE)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Stalks and residue fields at a point of an affine chart -/

/-- **The residue field at a closed point of an affine scheme is a quotient of the base.** If a
ring map `φ : R ⟶ B` is surjective onto `B/z` for a maximal prime `z` of `B`, then the composite
of `φ` with the canonical map into the stalk at `z` and the residue map there is surjective. -/
public theorem surjective_comp_toStalk_comp_residue {R B : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : R ⟶ B)
    (z : Spec B) (hz : z.asIdeal.IsMaximal)
    (h : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk z.asIdeal).comp φ.hom)) :
    Function.Surjective (φ ≫ StructureSheaf.toStalk B z ≫ (Spec B).residue z).hom := by
  let : z.asIdeal.IsMaximal := hz
  let : z.asIdeal.IsPrime := hz.isPrime
  have key : StructureSheaf.toStalk B z ≫ (Spec B).residue z =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap B z.asIdeal.ResidueField) ≫
        (Scheme.Spec.residueFieldIso B z).inv :=
    (Category.assoc (Scheme.ΓSpecIso B).inv ((Spec B).presheaf.germ ⊤ z trivial)
        ((Spec B).residue z)).trans
      (Scheme.Spec.algebraMap_residueFieldIso_inv B z).symm
  intro y
  obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ :=
    (Scheme.Spec.residueFieldIso B z).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective y
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := (Ideal.bijective_algebraMap_quotient_residueField z.asIdeal).2 y'
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := h w
  rw [RingHom.comp_apply] at hr
  refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
  rw [key]
  change (Scheme.Spec.residueFieldIso B z).inv.hom
    (algebraMap (↑B) z.asIdeal.ResidueField (φ.hom r)) = y
  rw [← Ideal.algebraMap_quotient_residueField_mk, hr, hw]
  exact hy'

/-- **A point whose residue field is that of its image, over a closed point, is closed.** An
isomorphism of residue fields is in particular an algebraic extension, so this is
[Stacks, Tag 01TE] in the form the field `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_closed` asks
for: closedness of the chosen centre is a consequence of
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_residue`, not an independent condition. -/
public theorem isClosed_singleton_of_isIso_residueFieldMap {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ Z)
    (y : Y) (h : IsIso (f.residueFieldMap y)) (hz : IsClosed ({f y} : Set Z)) :
    IsClosed ({y} : Set Y) := by
  refine isClosed_of_isAlgebraic_residueField f y ?_ hz
  let := (f.residueFieldMap y).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral (Z.residueField (f y)) (Y.residueField y) :=
    Algebra.isIntegral_of_surjective
      ((ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective (f.residueFieldMap y)).mp h).2
  exact Algebra.IsIntegral.isAlgebraic

/-! ### A point of a standard affine chart of a blowup -/

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {I : X.IdealSheafData} {U : X.affineOpens} {a : I.ideal U}

/-- The coordinate ring `Γ(X, U)[I(U)/a]` of the standard affine chart of the blowup of `X` in
`I` attached to a section `a` of `I` on an affine open `U`: the source of
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι`. -/
public abbrev blowupChartRing (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U) :
    Type u :=
  affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U) (a : X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1))
    (Localization.Away (a : X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)))

/-- Every point of the spectrum of the affine blowup algebra lands in the standard chart of the
blowup attached to `a` — the membership hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0BFL], here automatic. -/
public theorem blowupChartι_mem_range_relativeProjChart
    (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a))) :
    letI := (reesSituation I).sectionRingGradedRing U.1
    letI := (reesSituation I).sectionRingGradingGradedRing U.1
    blowupChartι I U a z ∈ Set.range
      ((Proj.basicOpen ((reesSituation I).sectionRingGrading U.1)
        (reesDegreeOne I U a).1).ι ≫
        Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjChart (reesSituation I) U) :=
  ⟨(affineBlowupStandardOpenIso I U a).hom z, rfl⟩

/-- The image in the base of a point of the standard chart at `a` is its image under `Spec` of
the structure map of the affine blowup algebra, that is, the prime it contracts to. -/
public theorem blowUpToBase_blowupChartι (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a))) :
    blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) =
      U.2.fromSpec (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1))
        (blowupChartRing I U a))) z) := by
  have h := congrArg (fun f => f z) (blowupChartι_comp_blowUpToBase I U a)
  rwa [Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply] at h

/-- **The stalk of the blowup at a point of the standard chart at `a` is the local ring of the
chart ring there.** The stalk map of the chart is an isomorphism, the chart being an open
immersion, and under it the map induced on stalks by the blowup morphism is the structure map of
the affine blowup algebra followed by its localization at the point.

This is the identification of the stalk at a point of the chart with the chart ring, in the form
the exceptional and residue-field conditions of `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep` consume. -/
public theorem germ_comp_stalkMap_blowupChartι (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a)))
    (hz : blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) ∈ U.1) :
    X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z)) hz ≫
        (blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z) ≫
        (blowupChartι I U a).stalkMap z =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)) (blowupChartRing I U a)) ≫
        StructureSheaf.toStalk _ z := by
  -- The statement is proved for an abstract chart, so that the elaborator never has to unfold
  -- the coordinate ring of this one: the concrete instance of the argument below does not fit
  -- one heartbeat budget.
  have key : ∀ (B : CommRingCat.{u}) (j : Spec B ⟶ blowUp I) (q : Γ(X, U.1) ⟶ B),
      j ≫ blowUpToBase I = Spec.map q ≫ U.2.fromSpec →
      ∀ (w : Spec B) (hw : blowUpToBase I (j w) ∈ U.1),
        X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (j w)) hw ≫
            (blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (j w) ≫ j.stalkMap w =
          q ≫ StructureSheaf.toStalk B w := by
    intro B j q hj w hw
    let : IsOpenImmersion U.2.fromSpec := IsAffineOpen.isOpenImmersion_fromSpec U.2
    apply Spec.map_injective
    apply (cancel_mono U.2.fromSpec).mp
    simp only [Spec.map_comp, Category.assoc]
    rw [show Spec.map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (j w)) hw) ≫ U.2.fromSpec =
      X.fromSpecStalk (blowUpToBase I (j w)) from U.2.fromSpecStalk_eq_fromSpecStalk hw]
    rw [Scheme.SpecMap_stalkMap_fromSpecStalk, ← Category.assoc,
      Scheme.SpecMap_stalkMap_fromSpecStalk, Category.assoc, hj, Spec.fromSpecStalk_eq']
    exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun v => v ≫ U.2.fromSpec) (Spec.map_comp q (StructureSheaf.toStalk B w)).symm)
  exact key _ (blowupChartι I U a) _ (blowupChartι_comp_blowUpToBase I U a) z hz

/-! ### The conditions on the centre of the next blowup, at a point of a chart -/

/-- The map from the sections over `U` to the residue field at a point of the standard chart at
`a`, read through the chart ring: it is the structure map of the affine blowup algebra followed by
the residue map of the chart ring at the point.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.germ_comp_stalkMap_blowupChartι` composed with the residue maps on
both sides; it is a separate declaration because the two statements together do not fit one
heartbeat budget. -/
public theorem germ_comp_stalkMap_comp_residue_comp_residueFieldMap_blowupChartι
    (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a)))
    (hz : blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) ∈ U.1) :
    (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z)) hz ≫
          (blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z) ≫
          (blowUp I).residue (blowupChartι I U a z)) ≫
        (blowupChartι I U a).residueFieldMap z =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)) (blowupChartRing I U a)) ≫
        StructureSheaf.toStalk _ z ≫ (Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a))).residue z := by
  have htr := congrArg (fun t => t ≫ (Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a))).residue z)
    (germ_comp_stalkMap_blowupChartι z hz)
  simp only [Category.assoc] at htr
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [Scheme.residue_residueFieldMap, htr]
  exact Category.assoc _ _ _

/-- The sections over `U` generate the residue field at a point of the standard chart at `a`, as
soon as the point is a maximal prime of the chart ring whose quotient is generated by them: the
hypothesis of `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_germ_residue`. -/
public theorem surjective_germ_comp_stalkMap_comp_residue_blowupChartι
    (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a)))
    (hz : blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) ∈ U.1) (hmax : z.asIdeal.IsMaximal)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk z.asIdeal).comp
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)) (blowupChartRing I U a)))) :
    Function.Surjective
      (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z)) hz ≫
        (blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z) ≫
        (blowUp I).residue (blowupChartι I U a z)).hom := by
  have hbij : Function.Bijective ((blowupChartι I U a).residueFieldMap z).hom :=
    (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).mp inferInstance
  have h1 : Function.Surjective
      ((X.presheaf.germ U.1 (blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z)) hz ≫
            (blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z) ≫
            (blowUp I).residue (blowupChartι I U a z)) ≫
          (blowupChartι I U a).residueFieldMap z).hom := by
    rw [germ_comp_stalkMap_comp_residue_comp_residueFieldMap_blowupChartι z hz]
    exact surjective_comp_toStalk_comp_residue _ z hmax hsurj
  rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.coe_comp] at h1
  exact h1.of_comp_left hbij.1

/-- **The residue field at a point of the standard chart at `a` is the residue field of its image
in the base**, as soon as the point is a maximal prime of the chart ring whose quotient is
generated by the sections over `U`. This is the condition
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_residue` asks for. -/
public theorem isIso_residueFieldMap_blowupChartι (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a)))
    (hz : blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) ∈ U.1) (hmax : z.asIdeal.IsMaximal)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk z.asIdeal).comp
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)) (blowupChartRing I U a)))) :
    IsIso ((blowUpToBase I).residueFieldMap (blowupChartι I U a z)) :=
  isIso_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_germ_residue (blowUpToBase I) (blowupChartι I U a z) U.1 hz
    (surjective_germ_comp_stalkMap_comp_residue_blowupChartι z hz hmax hsurj)

/-- **The exceptional condition at a point of the standard chart at `a`.** The extension to the
local ring at a point of the chart of an ideal inducing the maximal ideal downstairs is generated
by the image of the germ of `a`: the chart-membership hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0BFL] is
automatic for a point of the chart. -/
public theorem map_maximalIdeal_eq_span_germ_blowupChartι {p : X}
    (hI : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I p = maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p))
    (hpU : p ∈ U.1) (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing I U a)))
    (hq : blowUpToBase I (blowupChartι I U a z) = p) :
    Ideal.map ((blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z)).hom
        (hq.symm ▸ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) =
      Ideal.span {((blowUpToBase I).stalkMap (blowupChartι I U a z)).hom
                    (hq.symm ▸ X.presheaf.germ U.1 p hpU (a : Γ(X, U.1)))} :=
  map_maximalIdeal_eq_span_germ_of_mem_blowupChart I hI U hpU a hq
    (blowupChartι_mem_range_relativeProjChart z)

namespace PointBlowupStage

variable {P : (Y : Scheme.{u}) → (q : Y) → Y.presheaf.stalk q → Prop}

/-- **The chart step: a centre for the next blowup, with four of the five conditions a rule has
to satisfy.** Let `d` be a stage of a sequence of blowups at closed points whose chosen element
is the germ at the centre of a section `a` of the vanishing ideal of the centre on an affine open
`U`, and let `z` be a maximal prime of the coordinate ring `Γ(d.scheme, U)[centre/a]` of the
standard chart attached to `a` which contracts to the prime of the centre and whose quotient is
generated by the sections over `U`. Then the corresponding point `q` of the blowup

* lies over the centre, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_over`;
* is a closed point, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_closed`;
* has the residue field of the stage, which is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_residue`;
* cuts the exceptional divisor out by the image of the chosen element, which is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_exceptional`.

What a rule additionally requires is the carried property at `q`, which for a rational double
point is the statement that the local ring there is again the ring of a Situation 0BGC; that is
not a condition on the chart ring and is not supplied here. -/
public theorem exists_next_of_chart (d : PointBlowupStage P)
    (U : d.scheme.affineOpens) (hpU : d.point ∈ U.1) (a : d.centre.ideal U)
    (hgerm : d.scheme.presheaf.germ U.1 d.point hpU (a : Γ(d.scheme, U.1)) = d.elem)
    (z : Spec (.of (blowupChartRing d.centre U a))) (hmax : z.asIdeal.IsMaximal)
    (hcontract : z.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap (d.scheme.presheaf.obj (.op U.1))
        (blowupChartRing d.centre U a)) =
      (U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨d.point, hpU⟩).asIdeal)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk z.asIdeal).comp
      (algebraMap (d.scheme.presheaf.obj (.op U.1)) (blowupChartRing d.centre U a)))) :
    ∃ q : blowUp d.centre, ∃ hq : blowUpToBase d.centre q = d.point,
      IsClosed ({q} : Set (blowUp d.centre)) ∧
        IsIso ((blowUpToBase d.centre).residueFieldMap q) ∧
        Ideal.map ((blowUpToBase d.centre).stalkMap q).hom
            (hq.symm ▸ maximalIdeal (d.scheme.presheaf.stalk d.point)) =
          Ideal.span {((blowUpToBase d.centre).stalkMap q).hom (hq.symm ▸ d.elem)} := by
  have hq : blowUpToBase d.centre (blowupChartι d.centre U a z) = d.point := by
    rw [blowUpToBase_blowupChartι z,
      show Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (d.scheme.presheaf.obj (.op U.1))
          (blowupChartRing d.centre U a))) z =
        U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨d.point, hpU⟩ from PrimeSpectrum.ext hcontract]
    exact U.2.fromSpec_primeIdealOf ⟨d.point, hpU⟩
  have hiso : IsIso ((blowUpToBase d.centre).residueFieldMap (blowupChartι d.centre U a z)) :=
    isIso_residueFieldMap_blowupChartι z (by rw [hq]; exact hpU) hmax hsurj
  refine ⟨blowupChartι d.centre U a z, hq, ?_, hiso, ?_⟩
  · exact isClosed_singleton_of_isIso_residueFieldMap _ _ hiso (hq ▸ d.point_closed)
  · exact d.map_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_blowupChart U hpU a hgerm hq
      (blowupChartι_mem_range_relativeProjChart z)

end PointBlowupStage

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
